---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { loadSources, loadCatalog } from '../../scripts/catalog.mjs';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
const sources = await loadSources();
const entries = (await loadCatalog()).filter(e => e.listed !== false);
---
<Base title="Sources & authors" active="sources"><div class="container reading-page"><h1>One collection.<br /><span class="muted">Many great authors.</span></h1><div class="prose"><p class="lead">Jordan’s collection brings individual selections together without taking credit away from the people who made them. These are sources for curation, not a claim of affiliation or a ranking by popularity.</p></div><div class="source-list">{Object.entries(sources).map(([id,source]) => <section id={id} class="source-row"><h2>{source.title}</h2><p>{source.author}</p><p>{entries.filter(e=>e.sourceId===id).length} individual selections · {entries.filter(e=>e.sourceId===id && e.vendorPath).length} packages included</p><p><a href={`https://github.com/${source.repo}`}>Official repository ↗</a> · <a href={`https://github.com/${source.repo}/commit/${source.revision}`}>Reviewed revision {source.revision.slice(0,12)} ↗</a></p><p>{source.license}</p><a class="button secondary" href={withBase(`?source=${id}#catalog`)}>Browse these selections</a></section>)}</div><div class="prose"><h2>How an item earns its place</h2><p>A concrete use case, useful instructions or executable capability, inspectable source, clear credit, and manageable overlap with the rest of the collection. “Selected” means a curation decision, not proven personal usage, a security endorsement, or universal host compatibility.</p><p>Snapshots are pinned and checked by file hashes. Updates require a reviewed diff; the site does not silently pull the latest upstream instructions. Tools and packages with unresolved redistribution details remain linked.</p></div></div></Base>
